h_eps monotone on [0,1] for |eps| <= 1: True

=== 1. d = 2 projective: sum_i h(p_i) over random orthonormal bases ===
  eps=0.00: max |sum - 1| = 1.11e-15   (Born)
  eps=0.05: max |sum - 1| = 1.55e-15   -> valid non-Born frame function
  eps=0.20: max |sum - 1| = 1.55e-15   -> valid non-Born frame function
  eps=0.50: max |sum - 1| = 1.33e-15   -> valid non-Born frame function

=== 2. d = 3 projective (Gleason regime) ===
  eps=0.00: max |sum - 1| = 1.554e-15, median 2.220e-16
  eps=0.05: max |sum - 1| = 2.066e-02, median 6.295e-03
  eps=0.20: max |sum - 1| = 8.265e-02, median 2.504e-02
  eps=0.50: max |sum - 1| = 2.067e-01, median 5.868e-02
  functional equation: h(x)+h(y)+h(1-x-y)=1 on the simplex, with (1,0,0): h(1)+2h(0)=1, d=2 embedding h(0)=0
  => h(x+y) = h(x)+h(y) on [0,1] => (monotone) h(p) = p. Check residual of the equation for h_eps at random (x,y):
   eps=0.05: residuals [0.0095 0.0085 0.0184 0.0028 0.0026]
   eps=0.2: residuals [0.0381 0.0341 0.0734 0.0113 0.0104]
   eps=0.5: residuals [0.0953 0.0852 0.1836 0.0283 0.0259]

=== 3. d = 2 POVMs (Busch regime): effects E_k = (2/n)|phi_k><phi_k|, value v(E) = h(Tr rho E) ===
  trine       eps=0.00: max |sum - 1| = 6.661e-16
  trine       eps=0.20: max |sum - 1| = 8.246e-02
  5-star      eps=0.00: max |sum - 1| = 6.661e-16
  5-star      eps=0.20: max |sum - 1| = 1.513e-01
  tetrahedron eps=0.00: max |sum - 1| = 6.661e-16
  tetrahedron eps=0.20: max |sum - 1| = 8.270e-02
  Busch: additivity over all effect decompositions => v linear in E => v(E) = Tr(rho E), already for d = 2

