=== 5. premise audit ===
  Gleason: frame function on projectors of a SUPPLIED Hilbert space, dim >= 3, noncontextual (depends on P only)
  Busch: additive probability on the SUPPLIED effect algebra (all POVMs admitted as measurements)
  no-signalling: SUPPLIED tensor-product composition + the joint-weight rule applied to the composite
  contextual escape: Kochen-Specker forbids noncontextual value assignments, not contextual ones;
  Bohmian mechanics gets h(p)=p only via the quantum-equilibrium initial distribution (supplied preparation)
